post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
The daemon runs system-wide; no per-user setup and no "input" group
membership are needed. Start it with:

    systemctl enable --now three-finger-drag.service

Settings live in /etc/linux-3-finger-drag/3fd-config.json and are re-read
without a restart.

/dev/uinput only picks up its new group on the next boot. Re-running udev
against the live node instead does NOT work once logind has put a uaccess
ACL on it: chmod then writes the group bits into the ACL mask and leaves
the group entry empty, so the daemon still gets EACCES. To fix the running
system without rebooting, clear the ACL first:

    setfacl -b /dev/uinput
    udevadm trigger --action=add /dev/uinput
EOF
}
